The Core Insight
Individual tools are the right pattern when the tool does something the LLM can't — like calling an API, writing to a database, or running a process. They are the wrong pattern when the only variation is which fields you filter on.

With Observe and OPAL:

The LLM already understands IBM MQ concepts
discover_mq_context gives it the metric names and query syntax
execute_mq_opal_query lets it run whatever it figures out
You get zero code changes when new metrics appear in Observe. The LLM discovers them at runtime through discover_mq_context and immediately knows how to query them.

The same 3-tool pattern works for every other context provider in your platform too — bcp-context-provider, servers-context-provider, etc. If they all use Observe and OPAL, they each only need these same 3 tools.
